# The build context is uploaded on every build. Without this the whole repo went —
# 23MB, of which 4.4MB was .git, none of it used.
#
# An allowlist rather than a denylist: new junk in the repo cannot silently start
# being shipped, which is the failure mode a denylist has.
*
!go.mod
!go.sum
!pkg/
!services/
!web/
# Generated protobuf and gRPC stubs. They are committed rather than generated in
# the image, so CI needs no buf toolchain — but an allowlist means a new
# top-level directory is invisible to the build until it is named here, and this
# one broke every image build the moment the services started speaking gRPC.
!gen/

# Never ship tests, fixtures, or a local node_modules into an image.
**/*_test.go
**/testdata/
web/node_modules/
web/dist/
